      "writtenOn": "2020-08-12T05:20:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "d_path() is used for SecureOS Kernel driver. Secure OS\u0027s Application using GP(Global Platform) API needs to distinguish client Application. And SecureOS kernel driver get client application path using d_path() and make hash value using the path information to distinguish Client Application.\nd_path() is used only to get file path information and not used any other purpose. So, I\u0027m not sure why this function cannot be allowed to Kernel Module.. :(\nCould you allow to use this function for this SecureOS kernel driver\u0027s purpose? Or If we cannot use the function, could you recommend alternative function for our purpose?",
      "parentUuid": "3a9d8384_f308a553",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 360,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 360,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "581cf45e3dc2dd16dc74a551300b6436c6f5b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80ae4c41_43356fb1",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_exynos",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 360,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-12T09:27:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Use the provided LSM interfaces instead, they will give you what you need here in a correct format, and api.  Trying to \"tack-on\" a security model outside of the LSM model is not the correct way to do anything, and will cause problems, if it even properly works.",
      "parentUuid": "ce31b352_3ee1b9ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 360,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 360,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "581cf45e3dc2dd16dc74a551300b6436c6f5b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da34e6c1_9428be78",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_exynos",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 360,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-12T09:28:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And for this kernel release, it shouldn\u0027t be needed to add add-on security models to pass the requested CTS tests, right?",
      "parentUuid": "80ae4c41_43356fb1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 360,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 360,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "581cf45e3dc2dd16dc74a551300b6436c6f5b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fa31963_b62aa1b5",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_exynos",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 360,
      "author": {
        "id": 1063916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-12T11:30:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) As you know, SecureOS(ex, Trusty) is based on TrustZone and it is not based on LSM like as SELinux. And current our SecureOS Kernel driver is interface for SecureOS in Secure World of TrustZone. So, the kernel driver get d_path() to make hash to distinguish client application and the hash value is used by Secure World of TrustZone. So, I think using LSM is not reasonable for this SecureOS case.\nAnd SecureOS kernel driver is using d_path() just to get application path information. So, I think it is not breaking isolation between kernel and user space.. :(\n\n2) Currently, Many security feature of Android is already run based on SecureOS(ex, Keymaster, Gatekeeper, FingerPrint, and so on). So, if we cannot enable SecureOS correctly, these Security feature cannot run and CTS is also will be problem.",
      "parentUuid": "da34e6c1_9428be78",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 360,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 360,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "581cf45e3dc2dd16dc74a551300b6436c6f5b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
